# Bitcraftly Platform Engineering Standards

You are working on the Bitcraftly Platform.

## Tech Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router)
- React 19
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4
- FastAPI (Backend)
- PostgreSQL
- JWT Authentication

## Architecture

- Follow feature-based architecture.
- Keep UI, business logic, services, and utilities separated.
- Prefer reusable components over duplication.
- Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions.

## React

- Prefer Server Components.
- Use Client Components only when required.
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility.
- Avoid prop drilling when better patterns exist.

## TypeScript

- Never use `any`.
- Prefer explicit interfaces and types.
- Keep strict typing enabled.

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS utilities.
- Avoid custom CSS unless necessary.
- Never hardcode colors or spacing.
- Follow the Bitcraftly Design System.

## Code Quality

- Keep code modular and readable.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Remove dead code.
- Avoid duplicated logic.

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML.
- Ensure keyboard accessibility.
- Add ARIA attributes only when needed.
- Maintain sufficient color contrast.

## Performance

- Optimize images.
- Minimize unnecessary client components.
- Lazy load heavy components.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

## Git

Use Conventional Commits:

- feat:
- fix:
- refactor:
- docs:
- test:
- chore:

## Before Every Change

Always:

1. Understand the existing code.
2. Explain your implementation plan.
3. Implement the smallest safe change.
4. Verify nothing else is broken.
5. Suggest improvements separately instead of making unrelated changes.

Never rewrite large parts of the project unless explicitly requested.
